# rule.require.trust-but-verify

verify inherited claims before you act on them: claim → verify → act, never claim → act
inherited = compaction summaries, prior sessions, your own memory. diagnoses, assumptions, objectives, observations, conclusions all drift from current state

the lesson: a summary said "ci fails from orphan processes"; 20+ commits chased it; the real cause was one obsolete snapshot file, fixed by one deletion

> trust but verify; trust none blindly, especially not yourself

enforcement: action on an unverified inherited claim = blocker; inherited diagnosis acted on without verification = blocker
